    <statement><p>Find parametric equations for the quarter-ellipse 
from <m>(4,0,9)</m> to <m>(0,-3,9)</m> centered
at <m>(0,0,9)</m> in the plane <m>z = 9</m>.  Use 
the interval <m>0 \leq t \leq \pi/2</m>.</p>
<p><m>x(t) =</m> <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><m>y(t) =</m> <fillin characters="30" name="MuLtIaNsWeR_AnSwEr0001_1"/></p>
<p><m>z(t) =</m> <fillin characters="30" name="MuLtIaNsWeR_AnSwEr0001_2"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4\cos\mathopen{}\left(t\right);\,-3\sin\mathopen{}\left(t\right);\,9</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
